uild synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers recordings, and each named loader constructs `source` from `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` / `makeToolResult` rather than loaded recorded hook events (`corpus.ts:21-29`, `:42-53`, `:69-83`, `:97-105`, `:118-124`). The replay harness type is `source: AgentMessage[]` (`src/verify/replay.ts:39-42`) and it reconstructs lifecycle by inferring `agent_end` before a fresh user prompt and stamping synthetic entry IDs (`src/verify/replay.ts:111-147`). A filesystem search found no recorded corpus artifacts beyond `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` and `corpus.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2\",\"DoD-fixture-replay-M0-corpora\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"TC-6.1 mechanical replay path for current loaders: `replayCorpus` drives `mapMessage` -> `TurnAccumulator` -> `capture`, then compares durable events, `messages.listMessages`, and `turns.listTurns` (`src/verify/replay.ts:117-152`, `:432-457`).\",\"TC-6.2 mechanical determinism for current loaders: replay tests compare two fresh-thread logical event read-backs and same-thread re-replay dedup behavior (`test/verify/replay.test.ts:96-129`).\",\"TC-6.3 inspect surfaces: replay tests assert overview counts, last event position, failed derivations, and a capture gap visible through health (`test/verify/replay.test.ts:132-200`).\",\"Fixture-validity risk test for current fixtures: `validateCorpus` checks event shapes, tool-result correlation, closed turn, and rejects `makeTruncatedCorpus` (`test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts`).\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-6.1 / TC-6.1 recorded PI corpus input: current named corpora are synthetic stand-ins, not M0 recorded PI captures.\",\"AC-6.2 / TC-6.2 deterministic replay over recor