-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/state-machine.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 2 against AC-2.1 through AC-2.8, TC-2.1 through TC-2.9, current capture source, capture tests, LHC intake behavior, health surfacing, and configured pi-lhc gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id same-content events collide on idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized message to be recorded, AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events, and tech-design.md:329 requires fallback keys to be identical for the same logical re-delivery and distinct across different events using role/timestamp/content-hash. The implemented fallback in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:38-60 uses fallbackId default \\\"no-stable-id\\\", blockIndex, role, kind, and content, with no timestamp or source-event ordinal. Production message routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-357 may call mapMessage with only piSessionId when PI provides no entryId, and runtime-change routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-373 always passes only piSessionId. Focused checks showed mapMessage for two no-entryId user prompts with the same text returns the same key, and mapModelSelect for two identical runtime changes returns the same key. LHC skips duplicate keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unmappable PI hook input records no durable gap on writable threads\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.7 and TC-2.8 require a malformed or unmappable event on a writable thread to record a durable, queryable gap surfaced in health. The production hook path maps before capture: packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-357 calls mapMessage, then accumulator.onMessage, then capture. mapMessage has no default case at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:232-240; a focused check with role \\\"bogus\\\" returned undefined. That means onMessageEnd throws before capture can write a gap, and the generic guard at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:385-400 converts the failure into a recordedGap:false diagnostic. The existing TC-2.8 test covers a malformed MessageEventInput passed directly to capture at packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:135-178, not an unmappable PI message through the real hook path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.8\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-003\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Multiple unsupported tool-result parts share one omission key\",\"evidence\":\"Story risk reminder at 02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation.md:88-91 says unsupported image/file-reference parts must record an omission. mapToolResult iterates unsupported parts and emits one runtime_note per part at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:223-227, but each call includes the same toolCallId. eventKey then takes the toolCallId branch at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:47-49 and ignores blockIndex/content, so two omission runtime_notes for the same tool result get the same key. A focused mapMessage check for a toolResult with fileRef a.bin and b.bin produced two runtime_note events with identical key `pi:thread-1:tool:call_1:runtime_note`; LHC's duplicate-key skip path at packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216 means the later omission is not recorded.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"Story Risk Reminder: unsupported content omission\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id same-content events collide on idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized message to be recorded, AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events, and tech-design.md:329 requires fallback keys to be identical for the same logical re-delivery and distinct across different events using role/timestamp/content-hash. The implemented fallback in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:38-60 uses fallbackId default \\\"no-stable-id\\\", blockIndex, role, kind, and content, with no timestamp or source-event ordinal. Production message routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-357 may call mapMessage with only piSessionId when PI provides no entryId, and runtime-change routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-373 always passes only piSessionId. Focused checks showed mapMessage for two no-entryId user prompts with the same text returns the same key, and mapModelSelect for two identical runtime changes returns the same key. LHC skips duplicate keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unmappable PI hook input records no durable gap on writable threads\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.7 and TC-2.8 require a malformed or unmappable event on a writable thread to record a durable, queryable gap surfaced in health. The production hook path maps before capture: packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-357 calls mapMessage, then accumulator.onMessage, then capture. mapMessage has no default case at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:232-240; a focused check with role \\\"bogus\\\" returned undefined. That means onMessageEnd throws before capture can write a gap, and the generic guard at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:385-400 converts the failure into a recordedGap:false diagnostic. The existing TC-2.8 test covers a malformed MessageEventInput passed directly to capture at packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:135-178, not an unmappable PI message through the real hook path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.8\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-003\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Multiple unsupported tool-result parts share one omission key\",\"evidence\":\"Story risk reminder at 02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation.md:88-91 says unsupported image/file-reference parts must record an omission. mapToolResult iterates unsupported parts and emits one runtime_note per part at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:223-227, but each call includes the same toolCallId. eventKey then takes the toolCallId branch at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:47-49 and ignores blockIndex/content, so two omission runtime_notes for the same tool result get the same key. A focused mapMessage check for a toolResult with fileRef a.bin and b.bin produced two runtime_note events with identical key `pi:thread-1:tool:call_1:runtime_note`; LHC's duplicate-key skip path at packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216 means the later omission is not recorded.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"Story Risk Reminder: unsupported content omission\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1: covered for a user/assistant/toolResult sequence with assistant fan-out thinking -> text -> tool_call in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:43-87.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2: covered for the worked example; PI per-step turn_end hooks produce no LHC turn_end and agent_end emits one close in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:39-83.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.3: covered for two runs each using turnIndex 0, ordered by source-event order in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:86-118.\",\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.4: covered for parallel tool results arriving b then a and correlated by toolCallId in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:39-77.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.5: covered for isError tool results preserving error flag and content in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:80-105.\",\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.6: covered for graceful interrupt partial content, aborted disposition runtime_note, and closed turn in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts:29-65.\",\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.7: covered for same-key re-delivery skip and normal resume no historical re-fire in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:126-172 and packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:138-168.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8: covered for malformed LHC intake event direct-to-capture gap and unavailable store health signal in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:124-218.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: covered for a single model_select and thinking_level_select sequence producing ordered runtime_note events with new and previous values in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:90-121.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.1 / AC-2.6: distinct no-entryId same-content messages are not safely recorded because fallback idempotency keys collide.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: repeated identical runtime changes are not safely recorded because runtime_note fallback keys collide.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8: unmappable PI hook input on a writable thread is not proven to record a durable gap; code evidence shows it becomes a recordedGap:false diagnostic before capture writes anything.\",\"Story risk reminder for unsupported image/file-reference omissions: multiple unsupported parts in one tool result are not safely recorded because omission runtime_notes share a key.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"focused: mapMessage same no-entryId user prompts produce distinct keys\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"focused: mapModelSelect repeated identical runtime changes produce distinct keys\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"focused: mapMessage invalid role produces a durable writable-thread gap path\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"focused: mapMessage two unsupported tool-result parts produce distinct omission keys\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts fallback keys can collide for distinct no-id messages and runtime changes, causing LHC duplicate-key skips in production capture.\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts handles unmappable PI message failures through the generic hook guard before capture can write a durable gap on a writable thread.\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts emits duplicate idempotency keys for multiple unsupported tool-result omission runtime_notes under the same toolCallId.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Configured story and epic gates both pass, so the blocking issues are coverage/behavior gaps not gate failures.\",\"No material fake adapter, mock path, shim, or placeholder was found in the Story 2 capture production path; later-story NotImplemented modules remain out of Story 2 scope.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/011-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T09:48:49.627Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T09:53:27.297Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/streams/011-verify.stdout.log:10:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '560,570p' docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"- **Synthetic builders** (`test/fixtures/synthetic.ts`) — `makeUserMessage`, `makeAssistantMessage({ thinking?, text?, toolCalls? })`, `makeToolResult({ id, isError? })`, and event-stream builders for `session_start`/`agent_end` etc. These drive the lifecycle and turn-derivation tests where a precise hand-built shape beats a recorded one.\\n- **Deterministic ModelCall fakes** (`test/fixtures/model-call.ts`) — `fakeModelCallText(text)`, `fakeModelCallFailure(kind)`, and a per-kind router for multi-lane tests.\\n\\nFoundation tests (Chunk 0) verify these invariants before behavior chunks consume them.\\n\\n### Derived-State Provenance\\n\\nThis epic produces derived forms only via the closed-loop proof and fork requeue; it does not own provenance design (LHC does). The one connector-side rule: the fork path must not copy derived forms (I-2), so a forked thread's forms are always freshly derived and carry the new thread's provenance, never the source's. No provenance fields are added by the connector.\\n\\n### Mutation / Lease Semantics\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/streams/011-verify.stdout.log:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3. A fork produces a NEW thread seeded by replay and\\n     2\\t// never writes the source (tech design Flow 3). Story 4.\\n     3\\t\\n     4\\timport { readFileSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n     5\\timport type { MessageEventInput, OpResult, ThreadRef } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n     6\\timport type { ExtensionContext, SessionStartEvent } from \\\"../pi/types.js\\\";\\n     7\\timport type { LhcInstance } from \\\"../shared/instance.js\\\";\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\texport interface ForkInfo {\\n    10\\t  sourceThreadRef: ThreadRef;\\n    11\\t  forkEntryId: string;\\n    12\\t}\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t/** Detect a fork from PI's session tree when the session_before_fork hook is\\n    15\\t *  absent (Epic 1 fallback evidence). This function is called during\\n    16\\t *  session_start when we have a previousSessionFile but no pending fork from the\\n    17\\t *  hook. Returns fork info if the session tree indicates a fork, null otherwise.\\n    18\\t *\\n    19\\t * The fallback uses the previousSessionFile as evidence that we're starting a\\n    20\\t *  new session after an existing one (the fork pattern). The fork point is\\n    21\\t *  inferred as the end of the previous session. */\\n    22\\texport function detectForkFromSessionTree(\\n    23\\t  ctx: ExtensionContext,\\n    24\\t  event: SessionStartEvent,\\n    25\\t  sourceThreadRef: ThreadRef,\\n    26\\t): ForkInfo | null {\\n    27\\t  if (!event.previousSessionFile) return null;\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t  const previousEntries = readSessionEntries(event.previousSessionFile);\\n    30\\t  const previousIds = new Set(previousEntries.map(entryIdOf).filter((id): id is string => id !== null));\\n    31\\t  if (previousIds.size === 0) return null;\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t  const currentEntries = ctx.sessionManager.getEntries();\\n    34\\t  const sharedCurrentEntry = lastEntryMatching(currentEntries, (entry) => {\\n    35\\t    const id = entryIdOf(entry);\\n    36\\t    return id !== null && previousIds.has(id);\\n    37\\t  });\\n    38\\t  if (sharedCurrentEntry !== null) {\\n    39\\t    return { sourceThreadRef, forkEntryId: sharedCurrentEntry };\\n    40\\t  }\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t  const parentLink = firstEntryMatching(currentEntries, (entry) => {\\n    43\\t    const parentId = stringField(entry, \\\"parentId\\\");\\n    44\\t    return parentId !== null && previousIds.has(parentId);\\n    45\\t  });\\n    46\\t  if (parentLink !== null) {\\n    47\\t    return { sourceThreadRef, forkEntryId: parentLink };\\n    48\\t  }\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\t  return null;\\n    51\\t}\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\tfunction stringField(record: { readonly [k: string]: unknown }, field: string): string | null {\\n    54\\t  const value = record[field];\\n    55\\t  return typeof value === \\\"string\\\" && value !== \\\"\\\" ? value : null;\\n    56\\t}\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\tfunction entryIdOf(entry: { readonly [k: string]: unknown }): string | null {\\n    59\\t  return stringField(entry, \\\"id\\\") ?? stringField(entry, \\\"entryId\\\");\\n    60\\t}\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\tfunction lastEntryMatching(\\n    63\\t  entries: readonly { readonly [k: string]: unknown }[],\\n    64\\t  matches: (entry: { readonly [k: string]: unknown }) => boolean,\\n    65\\t): string | null {\\n    66\\t  for (let index = entries.length - 1; index >= 0; index -= 1) {\\n    67\\t    const entry = entries[index];\\n    68\\t    if (entry === undefined || !matches(entry)) continue;\\n    69\\t    return entryIdOf(entry);\\n    70\\t  }\\n    71\\t  return null;\\n    72\\t}\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\tfunction firstEntryMatching(\\n    75\\t  entries: readonly { readonly [k: string]: unknown }[],\\n    76\\t  matches: (entry: { readonly [k: string]: unknown }) => boolean,\\n    77\\t): string | null {\\n    78\\t  for (const entry of entries) {\\n    79\\t    if (!matches(entry)) continue;\\n    80\\t    const parentId = stringField(entry, \\\"parentId\\\");\\n    81\\t    if (parentId !== null) return parentId;\\n    82\\t  }\\n    83\\t  return null;\\n    84\\t}\\n    85\\t\\n    86\\tfunction readSessionEntries(filePath: string): { readonly [k: string]: unknown }[] {\\n    87\\t  let contents: string;\\n    88\\t  try {\\n    89\\t    contents = readFileSync(filePath, \\\"utf8\\\");\\n    90\\t  } catch {\\n    91\\t    return [];\\n    92\\t  }\\n    93\\t\\n    94\\t  const entries: { readonly [k: string]: unknown }[] = [];\\n    95\\t  for (const line of contents.trim().split(\\\"\\\\n\\\")) {\\n    96\\t    if (line.trim() === \\\"\\\") continue;\\n    97\\t    try {\\n    98\\t      const parsed = JSON.parse(line) as unknown;\\n    99\\t      if (typeof parsed !== \\\"object\\\" || parsed === null) continue;\\n   100\\t      const entry = parsed as { readonly [k: string]: unknown };\\n   101\\t      if (entry.type === \\\"session\\\") continue;\\n   102\\t      entries.push(entry);\\n   103\\t    } catch {\\n   104\\t      continue;\\n   105\\t    }\\n   106\\t  }\\n   107\\t  return entries;\\n   108\\t}\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t/** Extract fork info from a `session_before_fork` hook payload. The hook\\n   111\\t *  provides `entryId` and optional `position` identifying the fork point. */\\n   112\\texport function forkInfoFromHook(entryId: string, _position?: number): Omit<ForkInfo, \\\"sourceThreadRef\\\"> {\\n   113\\t  return { forkEntryId: entryId };\\n   114\\t}\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t/** Seed a forked thread by replaying the source's recorded events up to the\\n   117\\t *  fork point, through the normal intake path. The source receives NO writes\\n   118\\t *  (AC-3.1). Derived forms requeue rather than copy (AC-3.3).\\n   119\\t *\\n   120\\t * Replay reads events from the source thread, filters to those up to and\\n   121\\t * including the fork point (by entryId match on idempotency key), and writes\\n   122\\t * them through the instance's intake path. This preserves event order, dedup\\n   123\\t * keys, and all logical content — the seeded thread's read-back matches the\\n   124\\t * source's read-back through the fork point (AC-3.2).\\n   125\\t *\\n   126\\t * The forkEntryId is PI's entry identifier for the session entry at the fork\\n   127\\t * point. During capture, this entryId was encoded into idempotency keys as\\n   128\\t * `pi:<piSessionId>:<entryId>:<blockIndex>:<kind>`. We match events that\\n   129\\t * contain this entryId in their key (any piSessionId, any block/kind), then\\n   130\\t * include all events up to and including the turn_end that closes the turn at\\n   131\\t * the fork point. */\\n   132\\texport async function seedFork(\\n   133\\t  source: ThreadRef,\\n   134\\t  target: ThreadRef,\\n   135\\t  forkEntryId: string,\\n   136\\t  instance: LhcInstance,\\n   137\\t): Promise<OpResult<void>> {\\n   138\\t  const { intakeStream } = instance.sdk;\\n   139\\t\\n   140\\t  // Read all events from the source thread.\\n   141\\t  const events = await intakeStream.listEvents(source);\\n   142\\t  if (!events.ok) {\\n   143\\t    return {\\n   144\\t      ok: false,\\n   145\\t      error: {\\n   146\\t        errorClass: events.error.errorClass,\\n   147\\t        code: events.error.code,\\n   148\\t        reason: `fork source read failed: ${events.error.reason}`,\\n   149\\t      },\\n   150\\t    };\\n   151\\t  }\\n   152\\t\\n   153\\t  // Find the fork point event(s) by entryId match. The entryId appears in the\\n   154\\t  // idempotency key as `:<entryId>:` (Tier 1 format). We match any event whose\\n   155\\t  // key contains `:${forkEntryId}:` regardless of piSessionId.\\n   156\\t  const forkPointEvents = events.value.filter((event) =>\\n   157\\t    event.idempotencyKey.includes(`:${forkEntryId}:`),\\n   158\\t  );\\n   159\\t\\n   160\\t  if (forkPointEvents.length === 0) {\\n   161\\t    return {\\n   162\\t      ok: false,\\n   163\\t      error: {\\n   164\\t        errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   165\\t        code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n   166\\t        reason: `fork entryId ${forkEntryId} not found in source thread events`,\\n   167\\t      },\\n   168\\t    };\\n   169\\t  }\\n   170\\t\\n   171\\t  // Use the maximum eventOrder among fork point events as the initial cutoff.\\n   172\\t  // This ensures we include all events (including fan-out) at the fork point.\\n   173\\t  let maxOrder = Math.max(...forkPointEvents.map((e) => e.eventOrder));\\n   174\\t\\n   175\\t  // Include the turn_end that closes the turn at the fork point.\\n   176\\t  // turn_end events don't have entryId in their key (they're generated by\\n   177\\t  // the connector), so we need to include the first turn_end after maxOrder.\\n   178\\t  const turnEndAfter = events.value.find(\\n   179\\t    (e) => e.eventKind === \\\"turn_end\\\" && e.eventOrder > maxOrder,\\n   180\\t  );\\n   181\\t  if (turnEndAfter !== undefined) {\\n   182\\t    maxOrder = turnEndAfter.eventOrder;\\n   183\\t  }\\n   184\\t\\n   185\\t  // Filter to events up to and including the fork point (including turn_end).\\n   186\\t  const eventsUpToFork = events.value.filter((e) => e.eventOrder <= maxOrder);\\n   187\\t\\n   188\\t  // Convert EventRecord back to MessageEventInput for replay (strip server fields).\\n   189\\t  // Each event preserves its discriminated eventKind by construction from the\\n   190\\t  // recorded EventRecord, which carries the exact eventKind that was written.\\n   191\\t  const replayEvents: MessageEventInput[] = eventsUpToFork.map(\\n   192\\t    (record) =>\\n   193\\t      ({\\n   194\\t        eventKind: record.eventKind,\\n   195\\t        idempotencyKey: record.idempotencyKey,\\n   196\\t        actor: record.actor,\\n   197\\t        harness: record.harness,\\n   198\\t        payload: record.payload,\\n   199\\t      }) as MessageEventInput,\\n   200\\t  );\\n   201\\t\\n   202\\t  // Replay through the normal intake path into the target thread.\\n   203\\t  // This uses the same capture converter path, preserving all semantics.\\n   204\\t  const result = await instance.sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents(target, replayEvents);\\n   205\\t  if (!result.ok) {\\n   206\\t    return {\\n   207\\t      ok: false,\\n   208\\t      error: {\\n   209\\t        errorClass: result.error.errorClass,\\n   210\\t        code: result.error.code,\\n   211\\t        reason: `fork replay failed: ${result.error.reason}`,\\n   212\\t      },\\n   213\\t    };\\n   214\\t  }\\n   215\\t\\n   216\\t  return { ok: true, value: undefined };\\n   217\\t}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/streams/011-verify.stdout.log:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// Story 4 — fork as new thread. Tests fork detection, new thread creation,\\n     2\\t// replay seeding, source immutability, and derived form requeue behavior.\\n     3\\timport { writeFileSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n     4\\timport { join } from \\\"node:path\\\";\\n     5\\timport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n     6\\timport {\\n     7\\t  createDeterministicProvider,\\n     8\\t  inspect,\\n     9\\t  intakeStream,\\n    10\\t} from \\\"lhc\\\";\\n    11\\timport { createConnector } from \\\"../../src/index.js\\\";\\n    12\\timport {\\n    13\\t  makeAgentEnd,\\n    14\\t  makeAssistantMessage,\\n    15\\t  makeMessageEnd,\\n    16\\t  makeToolResult,\\n    17\\t  makeUserMessage,\\n    18\\t} from \\\"../fixtures/synthetic.js\\\";\\n    19\\timport { eventsAfterShutdown, kindsOf, startCapture } from \\\"../capture/support.js\\\";\\n    20\\timport { tempStore, type TempStore } from \\\"../fixtures/thread.js\\\";\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\tlet store: TempStore;\\n    23\\tbeforeEach(() => {\\n    24\\t  store = tempStore();\\n    25\\t});\\n    26\\tafterEach(() => {\\n    27\\t  store.cleanup();\\n    28\\t});\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\tdescribe(\\\"Story 4: fork as new thread\\\", () => {\\n    31\\t  it(\\\"TC-3.1 (risk: source-vs-derived): fork creates a new thread; source receives no writes\\\", async () => {\\n    32\\t    const started = await startCapture(store, \\\"/work/fork-source\\\");\\n    33\\t    const { connector, ctx, threadRef: sourceRef } = started;\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t    // Capture some events in the source thread with deterministic entryIds.\\n    36\\t    const forkEntryId = \\\"entry-fork-point\\\";\\n    37\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(ctx, makeMessageEnd(makeUserMessage(\\\"source prompt\\\"), forkEntryId));\\n    38\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(\\n    39\\t      ctx,\\n    40\\t      makeMessageEnd(\\n    41\\t        makeAssistantMessage({\\n    42\\t          text: \\\"source response\\\",\\n    43\\t          toolCalls: [{ id: \\\"call-1\\\", name: \\\"read_file\\\", arguments: { path: \\\"file.txt\\\" } }],\\n    44\\t        }),\\n    45\\t        forkEntryId,\\n    46\\t      ),\\n    47\\t    );\\n    48\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(ctx, makeMessageEnd(makeToolResult({ id: \\\"call-1\\\", content: \\\"file content\\\" })));\\n    49\\t    await connector.handlers.agent_end(ctx, makeAgentEnd([]));\\n    50\\t\\n    51\\t    // Record the source thread's event count for comparison.\\n    52\\t    const sourceEventsBefore = await eventsAfterShutdown(started);\\n    53\\t\\n    54\\t    // Simulate a fork: fire session_before_fork with the fork entryId.\\n    55\\t    await connector.handlers.session_before_fork(ctx, { entryId: forkEntryId, position: 10 });\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t    // print-mode --fork can report reason=startup; detection comes from the hook data.\\n    58\\t    await connector.handlers.session_start(ctx, { reason: \\\"startup\\\" });\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t    // The connector state should now point to a NEW thread (different from source).\\n    61\\t    const state = connector.getState();\\n    62\\t    expect(state).not.toBeNull();\\n    63\\t    if (state === null) return;\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\t    // The forked thread is a different file from the source.\\n    66\\t    const sourceId = (sourceRef as { threadId: string }).threadId;\\n    67\\t    const forkedId = (state.threadRef as { threadId: string }).threadId;\\n    68\\t    expect(forkedId).not.toBe(sourceId);\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t    // The source thread should have NO new writes — its logical read-back is unchanged.\\n    71\\t    const sourceEventsAfter = await intakeStream.listEvents(sourceRef);\\n    72\\t    expect(sourceEventsAfter.ok).toBe(true);\\n    73\\t    if (sourceEventsAfter.ok) {\\n    74\\t      expect(sourceEventsAfter.value.length).toBe(sourceEventsBefore.length);\\n    75\\t      // Event kinds and order should be identical.\\n    76\\t      expect(kindsOf(sourceEventsAfter.value)).toEqual(kindsOf(sourceEventsBefore));\\n    77\\t    }\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\t    // Shut down the forked session.\\n    80\\t    await connector.handlers.session_shutdown(ctx, { reason: \\\"shutdown\\\" });\\n    81\\t  });\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\t  it(\\\"TC-3.1 fallback: detects fork from PI session tree parentId chain when hook is absent\\\", async () => {\\n    84\\t    const started = await startCapture(store, \\\"/work/fork-tree-fallback\\\");\\n    85\\t    const { connector, ctx, threadRef: sourceRef } = started;\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t    const forkEntryId = \\\"pi-entry-source-user\\\";\\n    88\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(ctx, makeMessageEnd(makeUserMessage(\\\"tree fallback prompt\\\"), forkEntryId));\\n    89\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(\\n    90\\t      ctx,\\n    91\\t      makeMessageEnd(makeAssistantMessage({ text: \\\"tree fallback response\\\" }), forkEntryId),\\n    92\\t    );\\n    93\\t    await connector.handlers.agent_end(ctx, makeAgentEnd([]));\\n    94\\t\\n    95\\t    const previousSessionFile = join(store.dir, \\\"source-session.jsonl\\\");\\n    96\\t    writeFileSync(\\n    97\\t      previousSessionFile,\\n    98\\t      [\\n    99\\t        JSON.stringify({ type: \\\"session\\\", version: 3 }),\\n   100\\t        JSON.stringify({ type: \\\"message\\\", id: forkEntryId, parentId: \\\"root\\\" }),\\n   101\\t      ].join(\\\"\\\\n\\\"),\\n   102\\t    );\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t    ctx.sessionManager = {\\n   105\\t      getEntries: () => [\\n   106\\t        { type: \\\"message\\\", id: forkEntryId, parentId: \\\"root\\\" },\\n   107\\t        { type: \\\"message\\\", id: \\\"pi-entry-child\\\", parentId: forkEntryId },\\n   108\\t      ],\\n   109\\t    };\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\t    await connector.handlers.session_start(ctx, { reason: \\\"startup\\\", previousSessionFile });\\n   112\\t\\n   113\\t    const state = connector.getState();\\n   114\\t    expect(state).not.toBeNull();\\n   115\\t    if (state === null) return;\\n   116\\t    expect((state.threadRef as { threadId?: string }).threadId).not.toBe(\\n   117\\t      (sourceRef as { threadId?: string }).threadId,\\n   118\\t    );\\n   119\\t\\n   120\\t    const forkedEvents = await intakeStream.listEvents(state.threadRef);\\n   121\\t    expect(forkedEvents.ok).toBe(true);\\n   122\\t    if (forkedEvents.ok) {\\n   123\\t      expect(kindsOf(forkedEvents.value)).toEqual([\\\"user_prompt\\\", \\\"assistant_text\\\", \\\"turn_end\\\"]);\\n   124\\t    }\\n   125\\t\\n   126\\t    await connector.handlers.session_shutdown(ctx, { reason: \\\"shutdown\\\" });\\n   127\\t  });\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\t  it(\\\"TC-3.2: fork seeded by replay; read-back matches source through fork point\\\", async () => {\\n   130\\t    const started = await startCapture(store, \\\"/work/fork-replay\\\");\\n   131\\t    const { connector, ctx, threadRef: sourceRef } = started;\\n   132\\t\\n   133\\t    // Capture events in the source thread. Use deterministic entryIds for testing.\\n   134\\t    const sourceEntryId = \\\"entry-fork-point\\\";\\n   135\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(ctx, makeMessageEnd(makeUserMessage(\\\"prompt before fork\\\"), sourceEntryId, 1));\\n   136\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(\\n   137\\t      ctx,\\n   138\\t      makeMessageEnd(makeAssistantMessage({ text: \\\"response before fork\\\" }), sourceEntryId, 2),\\n   139\\t    );\\n   140\\t    await connector.handlers.agent_end(ctx, makeAgentEnd([]));\\n   141\\t\\n   142\\t    // Record the source thread's events as the expected fork seed.\\n   143\\t    const sourceEvents = await intakeStream.listEvents(sourceRef);\\n   144\\t    expect(sourceEvents.ok).toBe(true);\\n   145\\t    if (!sourceEvents.ok) return;\\n   146\\t    const expectedSeed = kindsOf(sourceEvents.value);\\n   147\\t\\n   148\\t    // Simulate fork at the current position.\\n   149\\t    await connector.handlers.session_before_fork(ctx, { entryId: sourceEntryId, position: 3 });\\n   150\\t\\n   151\\t    // Start the forked session.\\n   152\\t    await connector.handlers.session_start(ctx, { reason: \\\"fork\\\" });\\n   153\\t\\n   154\\t    // The forked thread should be seeded with the source events up to the fork point.\\n   155\\t    const state = connector.getState();\\n   156\\t    expect(state).not.toBeNull();\\n   157\\t    if (state === null) return;\\n   158\\t\\n   159\\t    const forkedEvents = await intakeStream.listEvents(state.threadRef);\\n   160\\t    expect(forkedEvents.ok).toBe(true);\\n   161\\t    if (forkedEvents.ok) {\\n   162\\t      // The forked thread should have the same events as the source through the fork point.\\n   163\\t      // The replay mechanism copies events with the matching entryId in their key.\\n   164\\t      expect(forkedEvents.value.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n   165\\t      // The forked events should match the source events through the fork point.\\n   166\\t      const forkedKinds = kindsOf(forkedEvents.value);\\n   167\\t      expect(forkedKinds).toEqual(expectedSeed);\\n   168\\t    }\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\t    await connector.handlers.session_shutdown(ctx, { reason: \\\"shutdown\\\" });\\n   171\\t  });\\n   172\\t\\n   173\\t  it(\\\"TC-3.3: forms requeue on fork (v1: no copy)\\\", async () => {\\n   174\\t    // This test verifies that derived forms are NOT copied from source to fork.\\n   175\\t    // In v1, forms always requeue on the fork target.\\n   176\\t    // The test requires the deterministic provider to have queued derivations.\\n   177\\t\\n   178\\t    let sdkMode: \\\"background\\\" | \\\"manual\\\" = \\\"background\\\";\\n   179\\t\\n   180\\t    // Start a source session with deterministic provider (so derivations run).\\n   181\\t    const connector = createConnector({\\n   182\\t      registryPath: store.registryPath,\\n   183\\t      newThreadFilePath: () => store.threadPath(),\\n   184\\t      parseLaunch: () => ({}),\\n   185\\t      buildSdkConfig: () => ({\\n   186\\t        ok: true,\\n   187\\t        value: { provider: createDeterministicProvider(), mode: sdkMode },\\n   188\\t      }),\\n   189\\t    });\\n   190\\t\\n   191\\t    const ctx = {\\n   192\\t      cwd: \\\"/work/fork-forms\\\",\\n   193\\t      hasUI: false,\\n   194\\t      modelRegistry: { find: () => undefined, hasConfiguredAuth: () => false, getAvailable: () => [] },\\n   195\\t      ui: { notify: () => {} },\\n   196\\t      sessionManager: {\\n   197\\t        // Provide session entries with entryId for fallback fork detection.\\n   198\\t        getEntries: () => [{ type: \\\"message_end\\\", entryId: \\\"source-entry-1\\\", position: 1 }],\\n   199\\t      },\\n   200\\t    };\\n   201\\t\\n   202\\t    await connector.handlers.session_start(ctx, { reason: \\\"new\\\" });\\n   203\\t    const sourceState = connector.getState();\\n   204\\t    expect(sourceState).not.toBeNull();\\n   205\\t    if (sourceState === null) return;\\n   206\\t\\n   207\\t    // Capture a prompt with matching entryId (for fork seeding) which queues\\n   208\\t    // prompt_smoothing derivation.\\n   209\\t    const forkEntryId = \\\"source-entry-1\\\";\\n   210\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(ctx, makeMessageEnd(makeUserMessage(\\\"queue some derivation\\\"), forkEntryId));\\n   211\\t    await connector.handlers.agent_end(ctx, makeAgentEnd([]));\\n   212\\t\\n   213\\t    // Drain to let derivations settle.\\n   214\\t    const sourceInstance = connector.getInstance();\\n   215\\t    if (sourceInstance) await sourceInstance.dispose();\\n   216\\t\\n   217\\t    // Check source has ready derivations.\\n   218\\t    const sourceHealth = await inspect.health(sourceState.threadRef);\\n   219\\t    expect(sourceHealth.ok).toBe(true);\\n   220\\t    if (sourceHealth.ok) {\\n   221\\t      // At least one derivation should be ready (smoothed_prompt).\\n   222\\t      expect(sourceHealth.value.owners).toContainEqual({\\n   223\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n   224\\t        kind: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n   225\\t        counts: { ready: 1, pending: 0, retrying: 0, failed: 0, blocked: 0 },\\n   226\\t      });\\n   227\\t    }\\n   228\\t\\n   229\\t    // Fork the session using the same entryId used for capture.\\n   230\\t    sdkMode = \\\"manual\\\";\\n   231\\t    await connector.handlers.session_before_fork(ctx, { entryId: forkEntryId });\\n   232\\t    await connector.handlers.session_start(ctx, { reason: \\\"fork\\\" });\\n   233\\t\\n   234\\t    const forkState = connector.getState();\\n   235\\t    expect(forkState).not.toBeNull();\\n   236\\t    if (forkState === null) return;\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\t    // Check forked thread's health before draining: forms requeue on the target\\n   239\\t    // as pending work instead of copying the source's ready rows.\\n   240\\t    const forkHealth = await inspect.health(forkState.threadRef);\\n   241\\t    expect(forkHealth.ok).toBe(true);\\n   242\\t    if (forkHealth.ok) {\\n   243\\t      expect(forkHealth.value.owners).toContainEqual({\\n   244\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n   245\\t        kind: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n   246\\t        counts: { ready: 0, pending: 1, retrying: 0, failed: 0, blocked: 0 },\\n   247\\t      });\\n   248\\t      expect(forkHealth.value.queue.queued).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n   249\\t    }\\n   250\\t\\n   251\\t    const forkInstance = connector.getInstance();\\n   252\\t    if (forkInstance) await forkInstance.dispose();\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t    await connector.handlers.session_shutdown(ctx, { reason: \\\"shutdown\\\" });\\n   255\\t\\n   256\\t    // Final verification: source and forked threads have different forms.\\n   257\\t    // The forked thread's forms were derived fresh, not copied.\\n   258\\t    const sourceHealthFinal = await inspect.health(sourceState.threadRef);\\n   259\\t    const forkHealthFinal = await inspect.health(forkState.threadRef);\\n   260\\t    expect(sourceHealthFinal.ok).toBe(true);\\n   261\\t    expect(forkHealthFinal.ok).toBe(true);\\n   262\\t    if (sourceHealthFinal.ok && forkHealthFinal.ok) {\\n   263\\t      // Both threads have ready derivations, but they are independent copies.\\n   264\\t      const sourceReady = sourceHealthFinal.value.owners\\n   265\\t        .filter((o) => o.owner === \\\"messages\\\")\\n   266\\t        .reduce((sum, o) => sum + o.counts.ready, 0);\\n   267\\t      const forkReady = forkHealthFinal.value.owners\\n   268\\t        .filter((o) => o.owner === \\\"messages\\\")\\n   269\\t        .reduce((sum, o) => sum + o.counts.ready, 0);\\n   270\\t\\n   271\\t      // Both have derivations - proving forms requeue and derive on fork target.\\n   272\\t      expect(sourceReady).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n   273\\t      expect(forkReady).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n   274\\t    }\\n   275\\t  });\\n   276\\t});\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/streams/011-verify.stdout.log:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \\\"fall through|normal launch|previousSessionFile|parentId|session_before_fork|fork_seed_failed|fork_thread_creation_failed|instance_init_failed\\\" packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:14:/** Detect a fork from PI's session tree when the session_before_fork hook is\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:16: *  session_start when we have a previousSessionFile but no pending fork from the\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:19: * The fallback uses the previousSessionFile as evidence that we're starting a\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:27:  if (!even