n-002.md:228:| TC-2.7 *(risk: idempotency)* | Re-delivered event dedups; normal resume re-fires nothing | replay same event twice; separately, resume | re-delivery returns `skipped`/`duplicate_idempotency_key`; resume produces no historical re-fire |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:236:> Hard-kill (no `agent_end`) is covered as a deterministic-boundary golden in `turn-derivation.test.ts`: open turn left open, tolerated as a no-op on reattach (no duplication of the recorded prefix).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:250:| TC-4.1 | Function resolves (provider,model) via registry, returns text | fake registry + complete returning text | returns `{ok:true,text}` for a single-turn message list |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:251:| TC-4.2 | Two kinds → different (provider,model) both route in one session | two assignments, two fakes | each call routes by its keys; both succeed |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:259:| TC-4.5 | Captured thread's queued derivation invokes fn + persists outcome | captured thread; fakes (one text, one failure); `drainSettled` | at least one ready derived form + one classified failure, both queryable via inspect/health |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:276:| TC-5.6 | Incomplete/unknown assignment fails loud at init | missing kind / unknown prompt / placeholder | construction throws actionable error; no placeholder masks it |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:282:| TC-6.1 | Each corpus replays to a thread whose read-back matches the fixture | chatty, tool-heavy, parallel, error, aborted corpora | read-back 