\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id, no-position capture events still collide on fallback idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded and AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events. The local production hook type keeps both MessageEndEvent.entryId and MessageEndEvent.position optional in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-39. The hook path only supplies fallbackId from event.position when entryId is absent in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:379-385, and runtime-change hooks do the same for optional position in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:402-415. If position is absent, eventKey falls to fallbackId \\\"no-stable-id\\\" in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:54-60. Focused checks failed: two no-entryId/no-position same-text user prompts produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:user:user_prompt:2cda7449dd14dbba9a0c9de9`, and two identical model_select events without position produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:system:runtime_note:fad453e343e63228f9ea2f15`. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events on this production path can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id, no-position capture events still collide on fallback idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded and AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events. The local production hook type keeps both MessageEndEvent.entryId and MessageEndEvent.position optional in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-39. The hook path only supplies fallbackId from event.position when entryId is absent in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:379-385, and runtime-change hooks do the same for optional position in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:402-415. If position is absent, eventKey falls to fallbackId \\\"no-stable-id\\\" in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:54-60. Focused checks failed: two no-entryId/no-position same-text user prompts produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:user:user_prompt:2cda7449dd14dbba9a0c9de9`, and two identical model_select events without position produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:system:runtime_note:fad453e343e63228f9ea2f15`. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events on this production path can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1: user/assistant/toolResult source-order capture and assistant thinking -> text -> tool_call fan-out are covered through the real hook -> converter -> LHC intake path in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:43-87.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2: the worked example records exactly one LHC turn_end at agent_end and PI per-step turn_end hooks produce none in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:39-83.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.3: two runs with repeated turnIndex 0 order by converter source-event order in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:86-118.\",\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.4: parallel out-of-order tool results correlate by toolCallId in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:39-77.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.5: tool result isError and error content are captured without drop in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:80-105.\",\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.6: graceful interrupt partial content, aborted disposition runtime_note, and complete-but-aborted turn close are covered in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts:29-65.\",\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.7: stable-key re-delivery skips and normal resume without historical re-fire are covered for entryId/source-position-backed cases in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:145-191 and packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:138-168.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8: malformed writable-thread input records a durable capture gap surfaced in health, unavailable store records health signal with no thrown hook exception, and unmappable hook input records a gap in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:140-276.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: model_select and thinking_level_select produce ordered runtime_note events with previous/new values in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:90-137.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.1 / AC-2.6 / TC-2.7: distinct no-entryId/no-position same-content message_end events are not safely recorded; focused evidence shows duplicate fallback idempotency keys.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: repeated identical runtime-selection events without position are not safely recorded; focused evidence shows duplicate fallback idempotency keys.\",\"Required proof that PI always supplies entryId or position to the production hooks is absent from the story, tech design, research evidence read, and local types; the implemented absent-position path remains live.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec tsx -e 'mapMessage two same-text no-entryId/no-position user prompts must produce distinct keys'\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec tsx -e 'mapModelSelect two identical no-position runtime changes must produce distinct keys'\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts relies on optional event.position as the only fallback discriminator when entryId is absent; packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts does not require that field, and packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts collapses the absent-position path to `no-stable-id`, causing duplicate-key skips in LHC intake.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Configured story and epic gates pass: 14 test files / 68 tests passed in each gate run.\",\"Prior unmappable-hook gap and multiple unsupported tool-result omission key issues are covered by current code/tests and were not reopened in this initial verification.\",\"No material fake adapter, mock path, shim, or placeholder was found in the Story 2 capture production path; later-story fail-closed inference stubs remain outside this story's capture scope.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/012-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T10:27:14.496Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T10:33:05.228Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/002-epic-reverify.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-reverify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"blocked\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"f18cd9cb-59e4-4d14-82c5-934c390e1d10\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8[1m]\",\"sessionId\":\"a7689c21-1739-4f71-b1a5-e967f006f0f9\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"a7689c21-1739-4f71-b1a5-e967f006f0f9\",\"operation\":\"epic-reverify\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"outcome\":\"blocked\",\"confirmedIssues\":[\"EV-001: Reload for no-flag and --resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection instead of reconstructing from the resolved thread id (AC-1.5). Implementation acknowledges this as an Epic-1 convenience with concurrent same-cwd limitation; no human-ruling artifact exists accepting this deviation.\",\"EV-002: Production --resume auto-selects most recent thread instead of resolving an operator selection (AC-1.7). Implementation acknowledges PI v0.79.2 lacks interactive input/selection surface; no human-ruling artifact exists accepting this deviation.\"],\"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\":[],\"readinessAssessment\":\"Epic remains blocked on two Story 1 deviations that require human ruling. Code evidence confirms both issues as documented. Gates pass but these are spec deviations, not test failures. No fix-batch or ruling artifacts exist to address these post-epic-review. The deviations stem from PI platform API constraints (no interactive selection surface), not implementation defects. Independent verification confirms the canonical review's findings remain current.\",\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Provide human ruling on EV-001 and EV-002. Both deviations are documented in code and verification artifacts with acknowledged limitations. If accepted, create ruling artifacts accepting these as platform-constrained deviations (similar to Story 0 and Story 4 ruling patterns). The impl-lead previously accepted these under standing authorization per team-impl-log.md, but no formal ruling document exists.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/002-epic-reverify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:45:41.641Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:47:08.256Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/007-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"01a3e81d-90a1-4cc8-85a8-22e6d9b9e34c\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5ea-fdf4-73e1-a3aa-8057551be95e\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5ea-fdf4-73e1-a3aa-8057551be95e\",\"storyId\":\"03-capture-verification\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-capture-verification\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Capture Verification\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/03-capture-verification.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/003-implementor.json\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Verified Story 3 against AC-6.1 through AC-6.3, the replay harness, fixture loaders, replay tests, supporting capture path, current artifacts, and configured gates. The replay mechanics and gates pass, but the required recorded PI corpus proof is still missing because the fixture substrate uses synthetic stand-ins and inferred lifecycle.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay fixtures are synthetic flat messages, not recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"Story 3 requires replaying recorded PI corpora and states M0 corpora are fixture inputs (`stories/03-capture-verification.md:6`, `:13`, `:24`, `:28`, `:33`). The fixture contract says `test/fixtures/corpus.ts` should load M0 captures, while synthetic builders are for lifecycle and turn-derivation tests (`tech-design.md:557-560`). Current `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4` states the loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers recordings, and each named loader constructs `source` from `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` / `makeToolResult` rather than loaded recorded hook events (`corpus.ts:21-29`, `:42-53`, `:69-83`, `:97-105`, `:118-124`). The replay harness type is `source: AgentMessage[]` (`src/verify/replay.ts:39-42`) and it reconstructs lifecycle by inferring `agent_end` before a fresh user prompt and stamping synthetic entry IDs (`src/verify/replay.ts:111-147`). A filesystem search found no recorded corpus artifacts beyond `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` and `corpus.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2\",\"DoD-fixture-replay-M0-corpora\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay fixtures are synthetic flat messages, not recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"Story 3 requires replaying recorded PI corpora and states M0 corpora are fixture inputs (`stories/03-capture-verification.md:6`, `:13`, `:24`, `:28`, `:33`). The fixture contract says `test/fixtures/corpus.ts` should load M0 captures, while synthetic builders are for lifecycle and turn-derivation tests (`tech-design.md:557-560`). Current `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4` states the loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers recordings, and each named loader constructs `source` from `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` / `makeToolResult` rather than loaded recorded hook events (`corpus.ts:21-29`, `:42-53`, `:69-83`, `:97-105`, `:118-124`). The replay harness type is `source: AgentMessage[]` (`src/verify/replay.ts:39-42`) and it reconstructs lifecycle by inferring `agent_end` before a fresh user prompt and stamping synthetic entry IDs (`src/verify/replay.ts:111-147`). A filesystem search found no recorded corpus artifacts beyond `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` and `corpus.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2\",\"DoD-fixture-replay-M0-corpora\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"TC-6.1 mechanical replay path for current loaders: `replayCorpus` drives `mapMessage` -> `TurnAccumulator` -> `capture`, then compares durable events, `messages.listMessages`, and `turns.listTurns` (`src/verify/replay.ts:117-152`, `:432-457`).\",\"TC-6.2 mechanical determinism for current loaders: replay tests compare two fresh-thread logical event read-backs and same-thread re-replay dedup behavior (`test/verify/replay.test.ts:96-129`).\",\"TC-6.3 inspect surfaces: replay tests assert overview counts, last event position, failed derivations, and a capture gap visible through health (`test/verify/replay.test.ts:132-200`).\",\"Fixture-validity risk test for current fixtures: `validateCorpus` checks event shapes, tool-result correlation, closed turn, and rejects `makeTruncatedCorpus` (`test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts`).\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-6.1 / TC-6.1 recorded PI corpus input: current named corpora are synthetic stand-ins, not M0 recorded PI captures.\",\"AC-6.2 / TC-6.2 deterministic replay over recorded corpora: determinism is proven only over synthetic `AgentMessage[]` fixtures with inferred lifecycle.\",\"Definition of Done: fixture replay for all available M0 corpora is not established because no M0 recorded corpus artifacts are loaded.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/verify/replay.test.ts test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"F-03-001: Story 3's verification proof path still relies on synthetic fixture stand-ins and inferred lifecycle rather than recorded PI hook corpus fixtures.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"openQuestions\":[\"Are the M0 recorded PI corpus artifacts available outside the current workspace? They are not present in the repository paths inspected.\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The previous shallow compare concern is closed in the current code: `replayCorpus` now reads and compares `messages.listMessages` and `turns.listTurns`, not only event counts or overview counts.\",\"No Story 3 runtime path was found that serves context to a model; the replay provider fails closed and health assertions verify failed derivations are visible.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/007-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T11:36:12.327Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T11:40:01.223Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/008-quick-fix.json:1:{\"command\":\"quick-fix\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result