{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614214904f968734e507f498b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive view of the implementation. Let me compile the epic review findings:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Stories integrate cleanly with no cross-story drift. The plain-data-only SessionState (state.ts) is consistently used across all flows, enforcing AC-1.3 structurally.\",\n    \"Turn derivation (Story 2) correctly integrates with lifecycle (Story 1) via index.ts — agent_end closes LHC turns, ignoring PI's per-step turn_end per AC-2.2.\",\n    \"Fork (Story 4) correctly builds on Story 2's replay machinery — seedFork uses intakeStream.messageEvents through the real converter path, not a bypass.\",\n    \"Inference routing (Story 5) correctly integrates with lifecycle (Story 1) — createModelCall is injected at initLhc construction, validates through PI's modelRegistry, and classifications map to LHC's ModelCallFailureKind contract.\",\n    \"Startup validation (Story 6) correctly validates all seven assignments (AC-5.1) and leaves capture running on failures (AC-5.3).\",\n    \"Idempotency key construction (Story 2) correctly tiers: entryId → toolCallId → responseId → fingerprint, with blockIndex/kind disambiguating fan-out — stable across re-delivery per AC-2.6.\",\n    \"Capture failure isolation (Story 2) correctly distinguishes writable-thread gaps (invalid_event → runtime_note gap) from store-unavailable (health signal) per AC-2.7.\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"The plain-data-only rule (AC-1.3) is structurally enforced — SessionState has no slot for PI ctx/session objects, making retention impossible in normal use.\",\n    \"Turn derivation correctly implements the PI-turn ≠ LHC-turn contract: TurnAccumulator opens on user_prompt and closes exactly once at agent_end, ignoring PI's per-step turn_end signals.\",\n    \"The idempotency key design correctly handles re-delivery across reload/replay with stable identifiers (PI entryId, toolCallId, responseId) before falling back to content fingerprint.\",\n    \"The converter's gap-recording path correctly isolates capture failures — writable threads get durable gaps, store-unavailable gets health signals, neither throws into PI hooks.\",\n    \"Fork implementation correctly uses two detection paths (session_before_fork hook and PI session-tree fallback) and seeds by replay through the real intake path.\",\n    \"The ModelCall adapter correctly implements the host-side contract: resolves through modelRegistry.find, classifies failures into LHC's kinds, and never returns empty_output (that's LHC's adapter responsibility).\",\n    \"Startup validation correctly separates shape validation (LHC-enforced at construction) from reachability probing (connector-enforced via modelRegistry.hasConfiguredAuth).\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"All 33 TCs have corresponding tests — 20 test files, 143 tests passing in pi-lhc gate.\",\n    \"All 7 architecture-risk tests from tech design are present: restart survival (Story 1), idempotency/retry (Story 2), adapter boundary (Story 5), atomicity/isolation (Story 2), source-vs-derived (Story 4), fixture validity (Story 3), concurrency (Story 5).\",\n    \"Foundation tests (Story 0) are present: corpus shapes, synthetic builders, ModelCall fakes, temp-thread factory.\",\n    \"Test fixtures correctly use deterministic ModelCall fakes (test/fixtures/model-call.ts) at the external boundary only — no module-to-module mocking inside src/.\",\n    \"Closed-loop test (Story 5) correctly proves the full capture→derivation→recorded-outcome loop via drainSettled, not just the ModelCall function in isolation.\",\n    \"Replay tests (Story 3) correctly use the real converter and intake path, then compare logical read-back (events, messages, turns), not just counts.\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholders in the production path. LHC SDK runs real against temp SQLite threads in tests and real thread files in production.\",\n    \"The ModelCall production path (inference/model-call.ts) resolves through ctx.modelRegistry.find, validates auth, and completes through @earendil-works/pi-ai when available — no fabricated completion text.\",\n    \"The verify/replay observeOnlyProvider fails closed (non-retryable) rather than fabricating derivations — correct for an observe-only epic.\",\n    \"All src/ modules exercise real LHC surfaces (intakeStream, threads, inspect, scheduler) — no mocking of LHC internals.\",\n    \"Hook handlers in index.ts use guard() to contain every handler, ensuring observe-only hooks never throw back into PI — correct failure isolation per AC-2.7.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"LHC retirement test needs SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS update for FORM_KINDS\",\n      \"evidence\": \"LHC verify fails 1 test (retirement.test.ts:62) because FORM_KINDS was added to SDK exports in Story 1 (A-8 registry work) but the checked-in SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS list wasn't updated. FORM_KINDS is a legitimate export (used by pi-lhc assignments.ts).\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"same-session-implementor\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Default model (gpt-5.4) shows unreachable in test environment\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Startup validation reports all 7 lanes unreachable with Reason: unknown_model for the default openai-codex/gpt-5.4 assignment. This is expected behavior in an environment without configured PI auth — validation correctly surfaces the misconfiguration, and capture continues running per AC-5.3.\",\n    